WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.080
We're having dried mackerel
for dinner tonight!

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.250
I stewed some veggies,
and we have chopped burdock root, too!

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
I'm proud of this meal!

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.010
MOMOCHI

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.010
Oh, I'm looking forward to it.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.840
I'm not at your level yet though,
Grandma Fumio!

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.140
Even now, you're a good cook, Tama.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.010
Right, Taka?

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.100
Yes.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.020
How can I put it?
There's a youthfulness to her cooking.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.600
Yes, exactly. A youthfulness.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:30.530
Fumi and I both always
look forward to your meals, Tama.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.780
Thank you, Grandma Takako!

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.030
Actually, my friend from school
complimented me on it, too!

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.040
The friend you're going to see today?

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.250
That's right!

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.750
Watch out for cars!

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:46.840
I will!

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:48.550
See you later!

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.170
- See you later!
- See you later!

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.770
U-Um...

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.310
Nice to meet you! I'm Tamate Momochi!

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.520
SLIMINESS OF AN EEL

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.850
Hana is always helping me out!

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:33.440
The way I hear it,
you're always helping Hana out.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.240
I'm Shion Kyouzuka.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:39.240
Please feel free to call me Tama!

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.490
Oh, then please just call me Shion.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.990
Shion!

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.000
Yes, Tama?

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:51.040
Shiotama is like a salty
ramen-flavored egg topping!

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.040
Really? It sounds delicious!

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.760
Are you a salty ramen
kind of person, Shion?

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.840
I like everything, but I have to have
my bamboo shoot condiment.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.930
I bet delicious bamboo shoots are made
from high-grade splittable chopsticks!

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.600
I bet they use cedar or cypress.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.140
Splittable chopsticks?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.940
Tama, please continue
to take good care of Hana.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.570
Sure! I'm not much good at anything,
but I promise I'll make her happy!

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.570
T-T-T-Tama?

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:22.410
You said you'd cook dinner
for us tonight, right, Tama?

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.910
If you need anything, take it from here.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.080
Thank you!

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.250
I can shred the cabbage with this peeler!

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.170
I've got this, too.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.760
You can easily make potato chips
at home with that!

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:37.710
And this!

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:40.130
Wow, you can make ground meat at home?

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.640
SAWAIZAMA STATION

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.640
Tama, you're amazing.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:45.720
Why?

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.980
I mean, you hit it off so easily
with people you've only just met.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:54.650
That's not because I'm amazing,
but because the other person is nice!

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.690
I-I see.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:01.320
And there's someone else who forcibly
leads everyone around by the nose.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:02.820
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.280
G-Good morning, Eiko and Kamuri!

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:07.290
Morning.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.750
Thanks for the invite.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:09.950
Thanks.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.920
Thanks!

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.380
Th-Thank you for coming!

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.960
Oh, boy, it's a beautiful day for a sleepover!

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.590
I brought video games, too!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.840
Tama, why are we staying over again?

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.470
To work at night and then play.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:26.600
Wrong.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.470
To stuff ourselves on Tama's cooking.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.810
I really am looking forward to that,
but it's not the reason for this.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:34.650
It's a study session, right?

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.570
You're the type who always sticks
to the original premise, Eiko!

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.910
Your cousin is out today, huh?

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.660
Yeah, a reunion.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:51.410
So I'm thrilled you guys are staying over,
but I'm also a little relieved.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.330
Being all alone would make
any of us kind of nervous.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.750
That's true.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.420
I've been afraid before
when I had to stay home alone.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.050
I kept thinking someone was behind me.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.090
That's like when I've taken a shower before

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.930
and had the feeling
somebody was watching me.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.970
Well, in most of those cases,
you were right! It was me!

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.560
Oh, that was you!

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.810
Now that you mention it, the other day...

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.020
I was studying in my apartment

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.820
when I heard something fall
to the floor behind me!

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.990
I nervously turned around and saw...

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.360
a...

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:27.780
sma...

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.160
Smoke?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:31.540
Small...

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.040
screw!

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.670
I kept thinking about
where that screw came from

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.880
and was so scared I couldn't sleep!

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.300
Because of a screw?

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.510
Something smells good.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.010
It's probably that eel restaurant.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:49.890
SPECIALTY
EEL RESTAURANT

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.140
That aroma is heavenly!

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:49.890
It sure is!

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.180
But when it comes to good smells,
nothing beats Eiko!

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.350
I'm not competing with eels,
so your consideration isn't necessary.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.610
Tama, do you know how to prepare eel?

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.480
I've never had the experience.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.570
But I've worked at an eel restaurant before!

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.820
You know how you get work experience
on a field trip in middle school?

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:10.910
I did that, too.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.080
That was a tough experience!

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.460
Amid the fragrant aroma of eel,

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:22.300
I worked my butt off,
and the meal awaiting for me...

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.970
...was the lunch box I brought from home.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.720
So lunch wasn't provided.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:31.050
You must've been in agony!

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.260
I was in total agony!

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:35.480
It's like, if I were an eel,
I would've been undercooked!

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:38.230
Don't eat eel that's been undercooked.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.360
Now if I'd been a popular woman like Eiko,

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:45.610
I bet they would've thrown in
one or two slimies!

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.740
Is a slimy a unit for counting eels?

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:52.280
Just talking about this
is giving me a craving for eel.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.870
But I'm in a bit of an economic pinch
this month.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:55.750
A pinch?

00:06:56.370 --> 00:07:00.830
In my house, I'm given
a monthly budget for food,

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.670
and I get to keep whatever's left
as pocket money.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.630
That's so responsible of you, Tama!

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.180
Yeah, but therein lies the problem.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.470
I learn new dishes,
find delicious-looking ingredients,

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:18.690
and feel like cooking
for my grandmothers.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:23.690
So I don't think I have enough left
to go to dinner with my family this month.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.900
I see. That's responsible of you, too, Tama!

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.820
Really? You're praising me?

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.370
Then keep going, shower me with praise!

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.410
Make a fuss over me!

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.910
Okay, I will! I'll make a fuss over you!

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:41.170
Tama, you really are incredible!
I admire you!

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.090
Tama is incredibly admirable.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.460
Th-That's really blunt!

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:51.010
Y-You can make a fuss over Eiko, too!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.760
What about her?

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.510
Look, she's right here.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.310
Good girl.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.270
Y-You're embarrassing me.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:01.810
This is rare for Tama.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.150
She's undercooked.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.190
This is agonizing!

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.780
Hana!

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.370
Hiroe!

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.160
You're all here!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.670
Long time no see.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.420
You're back to wearing sweats, huh?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.130
She's back to the sweats.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.760
You're right! I'm wearing sweats!

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.720
That's right! When did that happen?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:34.390
What am I doing?

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:37.430
I started with taking out the garbage,
then I went to the convenience store!

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.100
Then my discipline slipped by the day!

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:40.680
I'm sorry, Eiko!

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.520
Hit me until you get tired!

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:44.600
Um, I'll pass.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.860
Why, Eiko, why?

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:53.820
There you go.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.700
You look cute, Big Sis Hannen!

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.330
You look lovely, Hiroe!

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.200
Th-Thank you.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.210
Sticking to it is important.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.210
Yes, you're right!

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.340
This is like retempering
a dull sword of femininity.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:11.670
I have to work to maintain this form!

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:16.800
By the way, what's the occasion?

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:21.350
Is this one of those girls-only gatherings
I hear rumors about?

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.690
If only that were the case...

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.690
Unfortunately,
we're just having a study session.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.940
We've got semester finals coming up,

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:33.700
so I thought we'd have
a sleepover study session.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:36.700
That makes sense. So that's what it is.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:41.910
Then how about I help you guys study?

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.410
Really?

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:46.170
It'll be my way of giving back
for helping me increase my femininity.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:47.630
No need to be shy!

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.460
Thank you!

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.420
Yep!

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.720
You're smart, Hiroe!

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:00.180
What is this? I'm shocked!

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.680
<i>What did they think of me...</i>

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.600
<i>before this?</i>

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.020
I'm tired.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.440
I'm hungry.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:12.730
Yeah.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:16.070
But thanks to Hiroe,
we got a lot accomplished.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.450
I'm just glad I was helpful.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.080
The bath is ready.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:22.740
- Thanks!
- Thank you!

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.500
Then I'd better get going...

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.670
That's right!
I brought over bath salts.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.460
Is it okay if I put that in?

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:30.460
S-Sure.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.090
Hiroe, you can take the first bath.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.260
Uh, I'm...

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.340
Go on, take the first bath!

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.970
We owe you that much, Big Sis Hannen!

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.720
But, um...

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.890
Then take this.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.890
Please.

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:47.060
Okay.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.070
Why am I taking a bath...

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:55.320
in Hana's apartment?

00:10:58.070 --> 00:10:59.780
Oh, that's right, the bath salts...

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.960
Th-This is...

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:31.270
It looks yummy.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:33.980
But you can't eat it.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:37.940
Cut it out.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.660
<i>That's like when I've taken a shower before</i>

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:50.290
<i>and had the feeling
somebody was watching me.</i>

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.710
That's all the private bathtime you get!

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.880
T-T-Tama!

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.770
It's thick.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:13.190
I feel slippery.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:19.740
To go along with the gooey bath we had,

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.950
for dinner tonight, we're having
Tama's special chop suey!

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:25.490
And also rice
with a chop suey-like mix on top!

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:28.500
It's just like that!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.290
The bath was viscous just like that!

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.000
We all got boiled in there, huh?

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:35.380
Thank you for the food!

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:41.510
I think I know
what it feels like to be chop suey!

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:43.680
Chop suey's life isn't half bad.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:45.140
It's delicious.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:49.520
Are you sure it's okay for me
to eat with you guys?

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:51.020
Of course!

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:54.400
We made a lot of progress
because of you, Big Sis Hannen!

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:55.690
That's right.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:58.480
I didn't know you were so good
with academics.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:12:59.980
I may not look like it,

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:03.200
but I was the Student Council president
and at the head of my class in high school.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.450
I underestimated you!

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:07.950
More!

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.330
This is patting myself on the back,

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:12.410
but I was a popular Student Council president.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.920
The culture festival
for the years I was in office

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:20.550
CULTURE EXHIBITION

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:17.840
was called the "Culture Exhibition,"

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:20.550
using the kanji in my name!

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:23.090
I don't know if that means they loved you...

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.390
...or were messing with you...

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:26.970
More.

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.890
Let's play a game!

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.270
A game we can all play?

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:34.940
Like a driving game?

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.150
A dating sim!

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:37.150
Dating sim...

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:37.650
VIDEO 1

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.150
POCKET LOVE

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.650
Why me?

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.530
After all, it's a game
where you try to get girls into bed!

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.660
That doesn't answer my question.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:49.370
Do I push this?

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.120
That's right!

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:56.120
SUZUMI:
You play the innocent
from morning on, huh?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:56.120
RIRIA:
Good morning.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.750
I-It makes me nervous just watching it!

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.250
Y-Yeah.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:03.130
It's like hiding in the bushes
and spying on someone's love life.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:06.380
MOMOE:
The rooftop would be nice.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:06.380
RURUKO:
Hey, wanna play with me?

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.720
I recommend this girl!

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.050
What about this girl?

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:11.770
She's no good. She had a boyfriend
when she was introduced in the game.

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:15.100
Then you can't go out with her?

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.350
Oh, no, you can go out with her,

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:21.110
but you know, she has an ex-boyfriend.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.730
You should go with a girl

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:26.490
who always has and always will
love you and only you.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:27.490
Who always has

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:28.870
and always will...

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:31.830
Tama, you're scaring me.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:39.000
Favorability Rating

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.120
Now that's scary!

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:38.500
She just started playing,
and all the girls are in love with her already!

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.170
Thanks for putting out the futons.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:46.260
Not at all.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:49.010
You feel warm.

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:51.260
Kamu, are you ready to sleep?

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:56.730
I've used my head to study too much,
so I'm sleepy, too!

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.770
Yeah. Why don't we all go to sleep?

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.480
It's only 10:30.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:05.570
I don't think I've gone to bed this early
since elementary school.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.570
Well, I'm going to turn off the light.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:09.070
Okay!

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:13.910
I wonder what that sound was.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.120
Are you in the mood?

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.870
Sleepover means ghost stories, right?

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.630
G-G-G-Ghost stories?

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.250
Are we really gonna do this?

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.210
I'm sleepy.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.340
Let's start with Eiko.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:28.430
Okay.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:32.220
Um, I saw this online the other day...

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:32.850
Gulp.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.020
Huh? Was it a nurse?

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:37.850
Oh, well, whichever...

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:40.020
So there's this building

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:43.860
and a woman inside
who looks at you through the window...

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.860
Huh? Or was it a kid?

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:50.820
Well, various things happen,
and everyone dies by the end.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.490
Lazy.

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:55.330
That recollection is too faint to tell a story.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.960
E-Everyone dies—

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:00.960
- That doesn't even qualify as a story, Hana!
- Everyone dies...

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.500
Hey, do you have any stories, Kamu?

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:08.260
Mannequin legs decorate a stocking store.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:13.010
It's scary because it looks like
the legs are coming out of the shelves.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.850
When you think about it, that is scary!

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.600
There's no ghost, but it's scary!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:18.930
Scary.

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:24.230
I'll tell the next story.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:25.860
T-Tama?

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:31.820
It's the story about a girl who was hired
as a live-in servant in an old house.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:36.080
This sounds like a real story!

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:41.330
The rich girl of the house
and the servant girl were close in age

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:45.590
and lived together in harmony
like sisters.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:51.220
One day, when she was cleaning
the courtyard in her maid uniform...

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:54.430
Okay! And right here, we have
a still shot of the maid uniform event!

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:58.970
When she sensed something
and turned around...

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:01.390
There was an event still shot!

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:04.600
An event still shot!
A lavish feast of event still shots!

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:08.020
Event still shots scare me.
Event still shots scare me.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.990
Event still shots scare me.
Event still shots...

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.990
Hana, what are you scared of?

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.170
<i>I can't sleep.</i>

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:46.400
Hana...

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:48.520
Shush.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.530
Tama...

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.990
Sorry, I woke you up.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:55.780
Not at all.

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:57.660
You can't sleep?

00:17:58.870 --> 00:17:59.620
No.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:02.000
Um, then I found it again.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:03.500
This...

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:05.370
The screw.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.750
What should I do? What if it's
an important screw to something?

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.710
What if the ceiling falls in
while everyone's sleeping

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:15.510
or the pillar falls over
or the whole a-a-a-apartment collapses?

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:23.020
I don't think such important structures
use little screws like this, Hana.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:25.600
G-Good point.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:27.270
You're right.

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:29.360
Sorry, Tama.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.900
It's strange for me to be afraid, isn't it?

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:33.940
I see nothing wrong with it.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:37.660
What you like, what scares you...
It's different for every person.

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.160
Tama...

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:41.240
It's the same thing with dating sims.

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:46.670
The old friend, the tsundere,
the cold type, the older sister...

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:50.250
There was one
who had an ex-boyfriend, right?

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.710
Recently, there are "tomgirls"
who are boys that...

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:56.880
Well, it's complicated, so we'll set it aside.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:18:59.760
The girls in a dating sim
have different presents needed

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:03.680
to raise favorability rating,
different date places, different everything.

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:05.350
But that's a good thing!

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.900
If everyone liked the same thing,
and everyone was afraid of the same thing,

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:11.270
the game wouldn't be worth winning!

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:14.530
But I still say don't go with one
who has an ex-boyfriend!

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:21.240
Oh, I didn't mean to get fired up.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.700
To be honest,
when you first mentioned it,

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:27.910
I thought, "How can a screw
keep you up at night?"

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:29.920
I know, right?

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:32.290
But it is scary.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:34.420
You feel uneasy if you find something
like that in the middle of the night,

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:36.800
and don't have someone
to talk to about it, like,

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:41.680
"I wonder where this screw is from.
Isn't this scary?"

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.810
You said I was admirable, Hana,

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:48.690
but look at you,
doing your best to live on your own.

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:51.440
You're the one who's admirable, Hana.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:53.060
Tama...

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.110
Hana, I admire you.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:56.820
Good girl, good girl, good girl!

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.660
Is this kind of thing an event still shot?

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:03.910
Now you're getting it, Hana!

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:19.630
Good morning, Hana.

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:20.550
Good morning.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:22.050
Good morning!

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:23.050
Huh?

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:26.140
Kamu, your cheek's red.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:28.520
Oh, yeah. What is that?

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.190
Th-The curse of the screw?

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:32.440
Indentation from Eiko's nipple.

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.070
I do have tough nipples.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:38.780
The curse of the screw
made her nipples like a screw!

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:41.820
Why would the curse
pinpoint my nipples?

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:43.530
I've got it.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:45.580
It's the button from my top.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:48.830
O-Oh... Then it wasn't a curse.

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:51.330
A screw that curses nipples...

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.330
What kind of grudge would it have?

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.290
Speaking of screws... This!

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.050
A switch cover?

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:00.970
So this is where the screw came from.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.970
Good morning!

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:07.600
You're all early risers.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:11.350
Tama, your yukata isn't messed up at all!

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:13.190
Yeah, right?

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:17.230
They say I sleep like the dead.
More than even Tutankhamun!

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:19.820
Who's "they"?

00:22:52.790 --> 00:22:54.580
MOMOCHI

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:54.580
I'm home!

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:57.040
- Let's go out to eat!
- Let's go out to eat!

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:02.500
It's our treat.

00:23:02.840 --> 00:23:04.510
How about eel?

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:07.180
Eel? Sounds good!

00:23:08.430 --> 00:23:10.760
B-But are you sure it's okay?

00:23:11.010 --> 00:23:15.390
After all, you've been doing your best
with the cooking and budgeting.

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:18.270
That's right.
We're proud of our granddaughter.

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:21.520
Y-You're embarrassing me.

00:23:21.940 --> 00:23:23.480
So this is your reward.

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:24.530
Okay?

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:27.780
I bet you're hungry, huh?

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:29.860
Order a double-decker box!

00:23:29.860 --> 00:23:31.070
A double-decker box?

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:32.700
Order an omelette-wrapped eel, too!

00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:33.950
An omelette-wrapped eel!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:38.620
Thank you, Grandmas!
